<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Crimea</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Crimean peninsula</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Crimea is a peninsula on the northern coast of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a>. It was ruled by a succession of steppe powers and later by the Crimean Khanate, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from the fifteenth century. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> annexed Crimea in 1783 and fought the Crimean War there in the 1850s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/crimea.jpg" alt="Crimea" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Emirr, Spesh531 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crimea_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
